{
  "version": 3,
  "note": "Turns on tonal normalisation for every screening treatment, and rides an image-tools fix that stops engraving drawing sub-pixel lines. A screen carries tone through mark density, so it can only express the tonal range it is given; the procedural scenes deliver a compressed range (the arcade's wall sits at L* 0.85 and its sea at 0.45), which mapped to a narrow band of mark widths and read as flat texture rather than as a picture. With normalisation, engraved-colonnade renders a legible colonnade \u2014 arches, columns, statue and canopy all read \u2014 where before it rendered diagonal moire. Evidence: docs/evidence/perceptual/engraving-repair/.",
  "retune_reasons": [
    "cyanotype-arcade.halftone: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "engraved-colonnade.engraving: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "op-art-interior.line_screen: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "ukiyo-tide.halftone: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "stipple-massif.stipple: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "swiss-contour.line_screen: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening.",
    "ascii-field.ascii_mosaic: normalize the source's p1-p99 tonal span onto the full ink ramp before screening."
  ],
